    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "When you think back to when you were a child in school, did you already have trouble paying attention?",
      "targeted_symptom": "additional_requirement_1",
      "patient_response": "Oh, um... well, I suppose... yes. I mean, I really tried to be a good student, I promise I did. But, um... looking back, even in grade school, like definitely before I was 12 or so... my teachers were always telling my mother that I was bright. They always made sure to say I was a bright girl! \n\nBut... they also said I could be a bit careless. I'd, you know, accidentally lose my homework, or I'd forget the instructions they just gave us. And I guess I spent a lot of time just staring out the window instead of finishing my seatwork. I really wasn't trying to be a bad student or anything, my mind would just sort of drift off. \n\nI hope that answers your question... is that the kind of thing you were asking about?",
