    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "Do these attention problems cause trouble for you in more than one part of your life, not just at work?",
      "targeted_symptom": "functional_impairment",
      "patient_response": "Well, um... I guess you could say it happens at home, too. I mean, it's not like I'm a complete disaster or anything! I try my best to keep everything running smoothly. But, um... my husband has had to start handling all the bills and the important mail. I just... I kept misplacing the papers, or I'd completely forget what needed to be paid and when. I felt so awful about it, but he's been very patient. He just took over the reminders and things so I wouldn't have to worry.\n\nAnd at work... well, like I said, I'm a carpenter, and I take a lot of pride in my work. But lately, um... I've made a few little mistakes here and there. Just small things, mostly! But it has meant we've had to redo some work, and I think it's cost us a couple of commissions. The crew... well, they're great guys, but I think they're a little hesitant to let me handle the scheduling or the material orders right now. I can't really blame them. \n\nDoes that make sense? I hope I'm not making it sound worse than it is... I really do try my best to keep on top of things. Is that the kind of information you were looking for?",
